TI  - Protein-stabilized gold nanoclusters for colorimetric/fluorescence dual-mode 
      detection of organophosphorus pesticides.
PG  - 147115
LID - S0308-8146(25)04367-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.foodchem.2025.147115 [doi]
AB  - The residue of organophosphorus pesticides (OPs) poses a serious threat to the 
      environment and human health. Therefore, there is an urgent need to develop 
      sensitive, accurate, and environmentally friendly detection methods for OPs. 
      Herein, we constructed a colorimetric/fluorescent dual-mode detection platform 
      based on natural protein human serum albumin (HSA)-stabilized gold nanoclusters 
      (HSA-Au NCs), combining the intrinsic fluorescence properties and peroxidase-like 
      activity for OPs detection. The dual-mode detection strategy enhanced the 
      accuracy and reliability of detection by mutual verification of signals. 
      Moreover, benefiting from the biocompatibility of protein materials, HSA-Au NCs 
      were environmentally friendly, allowing OPs detection in real samples. By 
      integrating acetylcholinesterase, choline oxidase, and HSA-Au NCs on a cellulose 
      acetylation membrane, a smartphone-assisted sensor with high sensitivity, low 
      limit of detection, and environmental friendliness was developed. The sensor 
      demonstrated a low detection limit of 0.476 ng.mL(-1) for parathion methyl, which 
      was suitable for real fruit and vegetable detection.
